  "Description": {
    "Cost": 2505600,
    "UIName": "Kobold",
    "Id": "chassisdef_kobold_KBLD-X-C3",
    "Name": "Kobold",
    "Details": "This version of the Kobold was built by ComStar as a test platform for the Battle Armor C3i system. Though effective in combat, ComStar's engineers had to remove twenty percent of the armor used in the base suit and replace the existing weapon mounts with a single AP Weapon Mount. This unit is essentially a spotter for other friendly units, as its AP Weapon mount will only allow it to successfully engage conventional infantry.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Improved Communications</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 0.889</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#2aad3b>Can mount Omni units, can melee, can swarm.</b></color>",
    "Icon": "BA_Kobold"
  },
  "VariantName": "KBLD-X-C3",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "Squad",
      "BattleArmor",
      "OmniMech",
      "Trooper",
      "LightBattleArmor",
      "UsesAmmoSameLocationOnly"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Powered Infantry",
  "YangsThoughts": "The Kobold is a battle armor design that was collaborated on by the Free Rasalhague Republic, ComStar, and the second Star League. Originaly a project for a battlesuit that could mimic the capabilities of the Draconis' Kage, later the concept of shifted somewhat to a light armor that can still hold its own in battle. The Kobold can only jump up to ninety meters at a time, but it does boast enough armor to stop a Medium Laser. This armor is of the basic stealth variety, making it more difficult to target far away.",
